---
layout: atlas
---
<section class="hero page-width" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-statement">
      <h1 id="hero-title" aria-label="Augmenting how we perceive the world.">
        <button class="hero-reveal" id="hero-reveal" type="button" aria-label="Show Nahyun Lee’s portrait" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="hero-lines"
            ><span>Augmenting</span><span>how we <em>perceive</em></span
            ><span>the world.</span></span
          >
          <img
            class="hero-portrait"
            src="{{ '/assets/img/nahyunlee.jpg' | relative_url }}"
            alt=""
            aria-hidden="true"
            width="380"
            height="390"
            fetchpriority="high"
          >
        </button>
      </h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-aside">
      <p>
        I’m <strong>Nahyun</strong>, an undergraduate at Sungkyunkwan University studying
        <strong>Mechanical Engineering, Software Engineering, and HCI.</strong> I’m currently an exchange student at UMass Boston.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        My research investigates <strong>human perception and sensemaking</strong>, drawing on HCI, XR/haptics, and behavioral research.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        I aim to understand the <strong>cognitive and neural mechanisms behind perception and decision-making</strong>, and translate these insights
        into systems that <strong>augment human cognition.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-application">
      <div class="inline-links profile-links" aria-label="Contact and profiles">
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:leadtheworld@g.skku.edu"><span class="social-icon icon-email" aria-hidden="true"></span>Email</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leadtheworld/"
          ><span class="social-icon icon-linkedin" aria-hidden="true"></span>LinkedIn ↗</a
        >
        <a class="text-link" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=11pN9C4AAAAJ"
          ><span class="social-icon icon-scholar" aria-hidden="true"></span>Scholar ↗</a
        >
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/leadtheworld"><span class="social-icon icon-github" aria-hidden="true"></span>GitHub ↗</a>
      </div>
      {% assign announcements = site.data.atlas_announcements.items | where: 'enabled', true %}
      {% if announcements.size > 0 %}
        <aside class="hero-announcement" aria-label="Announcement">
          {% for notice in announcements limit: 1 %}
            <span class="social-icon icon-announcement" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="phd-note">
              {{ notice.body | markdownify -}}
              {%- if notice.url != '' and notice.url -%}
                <a class="notice-link" href="{{ notice.url | relative_url }}">{{ notice.link_label | default: 'Read more' }} ↗</a>
              {%- endif %}
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </aside>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <section class="home-news" aria-labelledby="news-title">
      <h2 id="news-title" class="sr-only">News</h2>
      {% assign latest_news = site.data.atlas_news.items | where: 'published', true | sort: 'datetime' | reverse %}
      {% for item in latest_news limit: 1 %}
        <article class="news-item">
          <time datetime="{{ item.datetime }}">{{ item.date }}</time>
          <h3>
            <a
              href="{{ item.linkedin_url | default: item.url | relative_url }}"
              {% if item.linkedin_url != '' and item.linkedin_url %}
                target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              {% endif %}
            >
              {{- item.short_title | default: item.title -}}
            </a>
          </h3>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
      <a class="text-link all-news-link" href="{{ '/news/' | relative_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >View all news ↗<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
      >
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="research-atlas" class="atlas-section" aria-labelledby="atlas-title">
  <div class="section-intro page-width">
    <div>
      <h2 id="atlas-title">My research <em>landscape.</em></h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="atlas-story page-width">
    <div class="atlas-sticky">
      <div
        class="globe-shell"
        id="globe-shell"
        tabindex="0"
        role="group"
        aria-label="Research globe. Rotates slowly; hover to pause. Drag to rotate or select a named research point. Press Space to pause or resume."
      >
        <canvas id="research-globe" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <div id="globe-nodes" class="globe-nodes" aria-label="Research projects">
          {% for project in site.data.atlas.projects %}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="globe-node"
              data-project="{{ project.id }}"
              aria-label="Explore {{ project.title | escape }}"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="project-preview"
              tabindex="-1"
            >
              <span class="node-core" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="node-label">{{ project.short_title | default: project.title }}</span>
            </button>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <aside id="project-preview" class="project-preview" aria-label="Research project preview" hidden>
          <div class="preview-top">
            <span id="preview-status" class="eyebrow"></span><button type="button" id="close-preview" aria-label="Close project preview">×</button>
          </div>
          <h3 id="preview-title"></h3>
          <p id="preview-summary"></p>
          <div id="preview-methods" class="preview-methods"></div>
          <div id="preview-links" class="preview-links"></div>
          <p id="preview-connection" class="preview-connection"></p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <button type="button" id="globe-rotation-toggle" class="globe-rotation-toggle" aria-controls="globe-shell" hidden>Pause rotation</button>
      <noscript>
        <p>Read the research on the <a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">Publications page</a>.</p>
      </noscript>
    </div>
    <div class="story-chapters">
      <article class="story-step overview-step" data-chapter="overview" id="chapter-overview">
        <p class="chapter-count">What guides my research</p>
        <h3>
          One world.<br>
          Different <em>experiences.</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          The same sensation or event can lead to different perceptions, emotions, and decisions. I build and study interfaces to understand
          <strong>how people construct those experiences and how technology can help.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          My questions connect <strong>sensory feedback, perception, and interpretation.</strong> Together, they point toward systems that augment
          human cognition.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="story-step journey-step" data-chapter="journey" id="chapter-journey">
        <p class="chapter-count">How the questions evolved</p>
        <h3>
          From sensation<br>
          to <em>interpretation.</em>
        </h3>
        <div class="journey-entry journey-sensory">
          <p class="journey-place">SCIGC <span>· Thermal haptics &amp; simulation</span></p>
          <h4>Can virtual worlds extend what we can experience?</h4>
          <p>
            I built thermal devices and an <strong>FDS–Unity pipeline</strong> for Mars exploration and firefighter training. The weight and
            complexity of hardware led me to ask how much physical detail a convincing experience really needs.
          </p>
          <div class="chapter-projects">
            <button type="button" data-select-project="mars">Mars exploration ↗</button
            ><button type="button" data-select-project="fire-dynamics">FDS thermal feedback ↗</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-entry journey-perceptual">
          <p class="journey-place">KAIST WIT Lab <span>· Perceptual cues</span></p>
          <h4>Can simpler cues make virtual touch feel real?</h4>
          <p>
            <strong>FeelSound</strong> uses granular synthesis for movement-coupled vibration; <strong>VR tactile illusion</strong> explores
            audiovisual cues for virtual touch. I led implementation, studies, analysis, and writing. Different responses to similar cues drew my
            attention to interpretation itself.
          </p>
          <div class="chapter-projects">
            <button type="button" data-select-project="feelsound">FeelSound ↗</button
            ><button type="button" data-select-project="audiovisual-touch">VR tactile illusion ↗</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-entry journey-reflective">
          <p class="journey-place">Future Computing Lab <span>· Interpretation &amp; Reflection</span></p>
          <h4>How do people interpret the same experience differently?</h4>
          <p>
            Moving from sensory perception to how people make sense of information and experiences, I explored how investors interpret uncertainty,
            decisions, and losses.
          </p>
          <p>
            I developed interfaces to <strong>recognize missing evidence before decisions</strong> and
            <strong>reflect on personal interpretations after losses</strong>. Through this work, I became increasingly interested in
            <strong>how people construct meaning from the same events.</strong>
          </p>
          <div class="chapter-projects">
            <button type="button" data-select-project="evidence">Missing Evidence ↗</button
            ><button type="button" data-select-project="facingloss">FacingLoss ↗</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-step future-step" data-chapter="future" id="chapter-future">
        <p class="chapter-count">The next question</p>
        <h3>
          What shapes<br>
          <em>an interpretation?</em>
        </h3>
        <p>
          My HCI research revealed a limitation:
          <strong>self-reports capture how people describe their experiences, but not necessarily how those experiences are formed.</strong>
          Individual differences led me to question the cognitive mechanisms behind perception and decision-making.
        </p>
        <p>
          I now aim to combine <strong>computational models, behavioral experiments, and neural evidence</strong> to understand how
          <strong>prior beliefs and emotions shape our interpretations.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Ultimately, I hope to build systems that help people
          <strong>perceive and interpret the world in more flexible, constructive, and positive ways.</strong>
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:leadtheworld@g.skku.edu"><strong>Let's exchange questions ↗</strong></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script id="atlas-data" type="application/json">
  {{ site.data.atlas | jsonify }}
</script>
<script id="atlas-blog-data" type="application/json">
  [{% for post in site.posts %}{"project_id": {{ post.project_id | jsonify }}, "url": {{ post.url | jsonify }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}{% endfor %}]
</script>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/research-globe.js' | relative_url }}" defer></script>
